--- 2026-09-26 ~18:30 PDT - CORRECTION: over-citation (operator: "it keeps citing the Large
    Catechism... ok a couple times but not over and over")

DIAGNOSIS: my previous change over-corrected. I had made a bracketed paragraph citation
MANDATORY on every doctrinal answer and required closing with the link every time. A 4B model
follows that literally, producing [Part II, 31] on every reply and a link on every message -
reads like a broken record. This was my error, not a pre-existing fault.

FIXES (all four prompt surfaces):
  - workspace/SOUL.md: section retitled "SPEAK IT NATURALLY, NOT LIKE A CITATION MACHINE".
    Most answers carry NO citation and NO url. Paragraph reference only occasionally, never
    twice in one conversation unless asked. Link only when it earns its place. Added
    "QUALITY OVER FREQUENCY".
  - workspace-sitebot/SOUL.md: brackets are now explicitly "for YOUR reference... most of the
    time a visitor should never see them". FAITH ANSWER retitled "(ONLY WHEN THE VISITOR
    ASKS WHO GOD IS)" + new DO NOT VOLUNTEER THIS ANSWER rule.
  - scripts/openclaw/chat-relay.py: step (2) back to one sentence of support; removed the
    inlined Part II quotes and the citation demand; added CITATIONS: no brackets, and
    "ALWAYS ANSWER THE QUESTION THAT WAS ACTUALLY ASKED".
  - ~/.local/bin/mastodon-openclaw-bridge.py: same; link now tied to the who-is-God case only.
  - workspace/memory/MEMORY.md: "cite the paragraph number" -> occasional use only.

SECOND BUG FOUND WHILE TESTING (pre-existing, not from my change): in a CONTINUING session
the model reused its earlier "JESUS CHRIST IS GOD" reply for unrelated later questions
("what is grace" got the who-is-God answer). Verified cause: the relay posts only the current
user message but the gateway accumulates history per session key, so a 4B model pattern-matches
its own prior output. Reproduced in a FRESH session: "what is grace" answers correctly. Mitigated
by the ALWAYS-ANSWER-THE-QUESTION-ACTUALLY-ASKED line; the underlying session carryover is a
model-capability limit, not a relay defect, and is recorded rather than papered over.

VERIFIED live, 4 turns in ONE continuing session (POST 127.0.0.1:18790/chat):
